  "suggested_action": "Most important, add an in-flight pilot or validation protocol for the foot-strap and left-hand tabletop-grasp method: standardize strap tightness, tabletop grasp position, tablet position, and body posture with photos or video, and measure or at least log tablet motion, body sway, strap tension, or grasp force if feasible, because [(Bieg et al., 2023-05)](https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/f3ff0bedae6143e46d2dcaca72405a0669643591) shows that consistent geometry is achievable but does not demonstrate that the proposed in-flight constraints are equivalent. Second, replace or supplement repeated-measures ANOVA with linear mixed models for continuous kinematic outcomes and a zero-inflated Poisson or negative-binomial model for error counts, including random intercepts for participant, target direction or item, phase, and interactions, with Holm-adjusted contrasts, mirroring [(Bieg et al., 2023-05)](https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/f3ff0bedae6143e46d2dcaca72405a0669643591) and better handling missing data and repeated trials. Third, increase the number of trials or provide a power analysis for 120 trials; [(Bieg et al., 2023-05)](https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/f3ff0bedae6143e46d2dcaca72405a0669643591) used 1056 trials per participant across six measurement points, and submovement decomposition plus peak acceleration and peak speed timing will require sufficient trials per direction and phase to estimate primary and corrective submovements reliably. Fourth, use the dominant hand or restrict participants to right-handed individuals, because [(Bieg et al., 2023-05)](https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/f3ff0bedae6143e46d2dcaca72405a0669643591) used dominant-hand tapping while the plan fixes the right index finger and left-hand stabilization, which could confound handedness with in-flight stabilization. Fifth, add throughput, error count or error rate, touch duration, and Fitts-law index-of-difficulty analyses alongside peak kinematics,